      "id": "39486888",
      "title": "Module Introduction",
      "sourceHash": "d387d8324ee16b951e8f7521663fef21576e92b1131a2b82bcb693241ae31ea7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 2.73,
          "en": "In this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.73,
          "end": 6.72,
          "en": "we're going to work on yet another new project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.72,
          "end": 9.45,
          "en": "and whilst working on this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.45,
          "end": 13.29,
          "en": "you will learn how to use Tanstack Query,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.29,
          "end": 18.29,
          "en": "a third-party React library, formerly known as React Query,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.23,
          "end": 23.61,
          "en": "so that's its old name, the new name is Tanstack Query,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.61,
          "end": 27.03,
          "en": "and it is a library that helps you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.03,
          "end": 32.03,
          "en": "with sending HTTP requests from inside your React app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.401,
          "end": 36.27,
          "en": "So it helps you with connecting your React frontend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 36.27,
          "end": 38.34,
          "en": "to a backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.34,
          "end": 39.99,
          "en": "Now, of course, in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.99,
          "end": 42.36,
          "en": "you already learned how to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.36,
          "end": 44.55,
          "en": "for example, with useEffect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.55,
          "end": 47.16,
          "en": "and using the built-in fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.16,
          "end": 51.48,
          "en": "that's provide by the browser, but in this section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.48,
          "end": 54.99,
          "en": "you will learn what exactly Tanstack Query is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.99,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "and most importantly, why you would use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 63.06,
          "en": "instead of using useEffect and fetch for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.06,
          "end": 64.144,
          "en": "And you will then learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.144,
          "end": 67.65,
          "en": "how to use this Tanstack Query library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.65,
          "end": 71.31,
          "en": "to fetch data and to mutate data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.31,
          "end": 75.33,
          "en": "so how to send, get, and post, and put, and delete requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.33,
          "end": 77.49,
          "en": "and all these things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "You will learn how to configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.32,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "and efficiently use this library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 86.55,
          "en": "and we will also explore many more advanced concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 91.02,
          "en": "like working with the cache that's provided by that library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.02,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "how it works, and how you can invalidate and change it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 98.28,
          "en": "We'll explore the topic of optimistic updating,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.28,
          "end": 101.55,
          "en": "what that is, and how you would implement it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.55,
          "end": 104.463,
          "en": "with Tanstack Query, and much more.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
